  "evidence": "Workleap's API overview says its user/group management data model is based on SCIM but \"The Workleap API is currently not SCIM compliant\"; provisioning runs through Workleap-run HRIS, Google Workspace, Microsoft 365 and Slack syncs, with API access and SAML SSO on Pro.",
  "notes": "New in 2026-09. Officevibe is now sold as part of the Workleap platform (officevibe.com/pricing redirects to workleap.com/pricing). No SCIM endpoint: user provisioning is Workleap-run directory sync from an HRIS, Google Workspace, Microsoft 365 or Slack (daily pull, one source at a time) on every tier, plus a proprietary REST API (SCIM-like but explicitly not SCIM compliant) for API provisioning and user/group management. Pricing is flat per organisation and billed annually: Standard from $4,999 USD, Pro from $11,999 USD, Enterprise (250+ employees) custom, so per-user fields and the multiplier are null. SAML SSO and API access are Pro and above (Standard has only Slack/Google/Microsoft 365 sign-in, which does not count); SAML is SP-initiated and set up via a support request. Okta's OIN 'Officevibe' app is SWA only.",
